module

public import Mathlib.CategoryTheory.Sites.Point.Skyscraper
public import StacksFrontier.Topology.Sheaves.Stalk.CommRingPushout

/-!
# The fibre at a point of a site of a pushout of sheaves of commutative rings

Let `(C, J)` be a site, `Φ` a point of it, and
```
R --f--> B
|g       |h
D --k--> Q
```
a pushout square of sheaves of commutative rings on `(C, J)`.  This file proves that the fibre
functor at `Φ` carries that square to a pushout square of commutative rings, and that
consequently every element of the fibre of `Q` is a *finite sum of products* `h(b) k(d)` of an
element of the fibre of `B` and an element of the fibre of `D`.

This is the site-level counterpart of
`Stacks.Sheaves.CommRingPushout.isPushout_stalkFunctor_map`, which is available only for a
topological space, and it is proved the same way: the fibre functor at a point of a site is a
*left adjoint*, of the skyscraper sheaf functor
(`CategoryTheory.GrothendieckTopology.Point.skyscraperSheafAdjunction`), so it preserves
pushouts.  The passage from a pushout of commutative rings to a tensor product is the
coefficient-free `Stacks.Sheaves.CommRingPushout.exists_list_of_isPushout`, which is reused
verbatim.

## Main results

* `Stacks.Sites.CommRingPushout.isPushout_sheafFiber_map` — the fibre functor at a point of a
  site carries a pushout square of sheaves to a pushout square, for any category of
  coefficients with products and colimits of the size of the point.
* `Stacks.Sites.CommRingPushout.exists_list_sheafFiber_of_isPushout` — every element of the
  fibre of a pushout of sheaves of commutative rings is a finite sum of products of elements of
  the fibres of the two legs.
* `Stacks.Sites.CommRingPushout.exists_ringEquiv_tensorProduct_of_isPushout` — a pushout of
  commutative rings is the tensor product, with the two legs as the two inclusions.
* `Stacks.Sites.CommRingPushout.exists_ringEquiv_tensorProduct_sheafFiber` — **the fibre of a
  pushout of sheaves of commutative rings is the tensor product of the fibres.**

## Implementation notes

`isPushout_sheafFiber_map` is stated for arbitrary coefficients rather than only for
`CommRingCat`, since nothing about rings enters it;  the ring content is confined to the
corollaries, which instantiate it at `CommRingCat.{w}` — the universe at which the point takes
its fibres, which is the only one at which the two instance hypotheses
`HasProducts.{w}` and `HasColimitsOfSize.{w, w}` are discharged automatically.

The two tensor-product statements are existential rather than a named isomorphism because the
algebra structures on the two legs of the span are the ones the span itself defines, through
`RingHom.toAlgebra`;  carrying them as `letI`s inside the statement keeps the tensor product
well-formed without committing the file to a choice of instance that a caller would have to
match.

The conclusion is phrased with a `List` rather than with a `Finset`, for the same reason as
`Stacks.Sheaves.CommRingPushout.exists_list_of_isPushout`: the summands are not assumed
distinct, and the induction over `TensorProduct.induction_on` behind that lemma appends.

**No `@[stacks]` attribute is placed in this file.**  Nothing here is a tagged result of the
source;  it is the input that the identification of the module underlying an algebra pullback
on the small étale site of an algebraic space needs, in the same way the topological file
serves [Stacks, Tag 01SA].

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 04K0](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/04K0)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 04K1](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/04K1)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits Opposite
open scoped TensorProduct

universe w v' v u' u

namespace Stacks.Sites.CommRingPushout

open CategoryTheory.GrothendieckTopology

variable {C : Type u} [Category.{v} C] {J : GrothendieckTopology C} (Φ : J.Point.{w})

/-- **The fibre functor at a point of a site preserves pushouts of sheaves.**  It is the left
adjoint of the skyscraper sheaf functor
(`CategoryTheory.GrothendieckTopology.Point.skyscraperSheafAdjunction`), hence preserves all
colimits. -/
public theorem isPushout_sheafFiber_map {A : Type u'} [Category.{v'} A] [HasProducts.{w} A]
    [HasColimitsOfSize.{w, w} A] {R B D Q : Sheaf J A} {f : R ⟶ B} {g : R ⟶ D} {h : B ⟶ Q}
    {k : D ⟶ Q} (H : IsPushout f g h k) :
    IsPushout ((Φ.sheafFiber (A := A)).map f) ((Φ.sheafFiber (A := A)).map g)
      ((Φ.sheafFiber (A := A)).map h) ((Φ.sheafFiber (A := A)).map k) :=
  H.map (Φ.sheafFiber (A := A))

/-- **A pushout of sheaves of commutative rings is generated by its two legs on fibres.**  Every
element of the fibre at a point of the site of the pushout of a span of sheaves of commutative
rings is a finite sum of products of the images of an element of the fibre of `B` and an element
of the fibre of `D`. -/
public theorem exists_list_sheafFiber_of_isPushout
    {R B D Q : Sheaf J CommRingCat.{w}} {f : R ⟶ B} {g : R ⟶ D} {h : B ⟶ Q} {k : D ⟶ Q}
    (H : IsPushout f g h k) (q : (Φ.sheafFiber (A := CommRingCat.{w})).obj Q) :
    ∃ L : List ((Φ.sheafFiber (A := CommRingCat.{w})).obj B ×
        (Φ.sheafFiber (A := CommRingCat.{w})).obj D),
      q = (L.map (fun p =>
        ((Φ.sheafFiber (A := CommRingCat.{w})).map h).hom p.1 *
          ((Φ.sheafFiber (A := CommRingCat.{w})).map k).hom p.2)).sum :=
  Stacks.Sheaves.CommRingPushout.exists_list_of_isPushout
    (isPushout_sheafFiber_map Φ H) q

/-- **A pushout of commutative rings is the tensor product, with its two legs as the two
inclusions.**  For a pushout square with span `f : R ⟶ B`, `g : R ⟶ D` and legs `h : B ⟶ Q`,
`k : D ⟶ Q`, there is a ring isomorphism `B ⊗_R D ≃+* Q` carrying the pure tensor `b ⊗ d` to
`h(b) k(d)`, the algebra structures on `B` and `D` being the ones the span defines.

This is the identification `Stacks.Sheaves.CommRingPushout.exists_list_of_isPushout` is read
off, stated in full rather than only through its consequence on sums of pure tensors;  it is
what a computation of the fibre of a pushout as a tensor product has to end in. -/
public theorem exists_ringEquiv_tensorProduct_of_isPushout {R B D Q : CommRingCat.{u}}
    {f : R ⟶ B} {g : R ⟶ D} {h : B ⟶ Q} {k : D ⟶ Q} (H : IsPushout f g h k) :
    letI : Algebra R B := f.hom.toAlgebra
    letI : Algebra R D := g.hom.toAlgebra
    ∃ e : (B ⊗[R] D) ≃+* Q, ∀ (b : B) (d : D), e (b ⊗ₜ d) = h.hom b * k.hom d := by
  let _i1 : Algebra R B := f.hom.toAlgebra
  let _i2 : Algebra R D := g.hom.toAlgebra
  have H' : IsPushout f g
      (CommRingCat.ofHom (S := B ⊗[R] D) Algebra.TensorProduct.includeLeftRingHom)
      (CommRingCat.ofHom (S := B ⊗[R] D) Algebra.TensorProduct.includeRight.toRingHom) :=
    CommRingCat.isPushout_tensorProduct R B D
  refine ⟨(IsPushout.isoIsPushout _ _ H' H).commRingCatIsoToRingEquiv, fun b d => ?_⟩
  have ht : (b ⊗ₜ[R] d : B ⊗[R] D) =
      Algebra.TensorProduct.includeLeftRingHom b *
        Algebra.TensorProduct.includeRight.toRingHom d := by
    simp [Algebra.TensorProduct.includeLeftRingHom_apply,
      Algebra.TensorProduct.includeRight_apply, Algebra.TensorProduct.tmul_mul_tmul]
  change (IsPushout.isoIsPushout _ _ H' H).hom.hom _ = _
  rw [ht, map_mul]
  exact congrArg₂ (· * ·)
    (congrArg (fun z : B ⟶ Q => z.hom b) (IsPushout.inl_isoIsPushout_hom _ _ H' H))
    (congrArg (fun z : D ⟶ Q => z.hom d) (IsPushout.inr_isoIsPushout_hom _ _ H' H))

/-- **The fibre at a point of a site of a pushout of sheaves of commutative rings is the tensor
product of the fibres.**  For a pushout square of sheaves of commutative rings with span
`f : R ⟶ B`, `g : R ⟶ D` and legs `h`, `k`, the fibre of `Q` at `Φ` is `B_Φ ⊗_{R_Φ} D_Φ`,
the isomorphism carrying `b ⊗ d` to the product of the images of `b` and `d`.

This is the site-level counterpart of the stalk computation that
`Stacks.AlgebraPullbackQcoh.isIso_comparison` runs on a scheme:  it is the fibre of the ring
pushout, which is one of the two sides a comparison of the module underlying an algebra
pullback with a module pullback has to be checked against. -/
public theorem exists_ringEquiv_tensorProduct_sheafFiber
    {R B D Q : Sheaf J CommRingCat.{w}} {f : R ⟶ B} {g : R ⟶ D} {h : B ⟶ Q} {k : D ⟶ Q}
    (H : IsPushout f g h k) :
    letI : Algebra ((Φ.sheafFiber (A := CommRingCat.{w})).obj R)
        ((Φ.sheafFiber (A := CommRingCat.{w})).obj B) :=
      ((Φ.sheafFiber (A := CommRingCat.{w})).map f).hom.toAlgebra
    letI : Algebra ((Φ.sheafFiber (A := CommRingCat.{w})).obj R)
        ((Φ.sheafFiber (A := CommRingCat.{w})).obj D) :=
      ((Φ.sheafFiber (A := CommRingCat.{w})).map g).hom.toAlgebra
    ∃ e : ((Φ.sheafFiber (A := CommRingCat.{w})).obj B ⊗[
            (Φ.sheafFiber (A := CommRingCat.{w})).obj R]
          (Φ.sheafFiber (A := CommRingCat.{w})).obj D) ≃+*
        (Φ.sheafFiber (A := CommRingCat.{w})).obj Q,
      ∀ (b : (Φ.sheafFiber (A := CommRingCat.{w})).obj B)
        (d : (Φ.sheafFiber (A := CommRingCat.{w})).obj D),
        e (b ⊗ₜ d) = ((Φ.sheafFiber (A := CommRingCat.{w})).map h).hom b *
          ((Φ.sheafFiber (A := CommRingCat.{w})).map k).hom d :=
  exists_ringEquiv_tensorProduct_of_isPushout (isPushout_sheafFiber_map Φ H)

end Stacks.Sites.CommRingPushout

end
